suggestion:
Suggestion 1. Consume leftover newline after reading integer. After reading the integer with `sc.nextInt()`, immediately consume the leftover newline character. Add `sc.nextLine();` right after `sc.nextInt();` to ensure that the subsequent `nextLine()` reads the actual line input.
```java
public static void main(String[] args) {
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
    int N = sc.nextInt();
    sc.nextLine(); // consume the newline character

    int count = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
        String s = sc.nextLine();
        if (s.equals("Takahashi")) {
            count++;
        }
    }
    System.out.println(count);
}
```

